
# Type the filename exactly as:   backups/.gitkeep
# (typing the "/" auto-creates the backups/ folder)
# Leave the file body COMPLETELY EMPTY — 0 bytes — then Commit to main.
# Its only job is to keep the empty backups/ folder alive in the repo until the
# first "Backup Now" from the Q admin build commits a real snapshot there.
# NOTE: GitHub's drag-and-drop uploader silently skips dotfiles — always use
# "Create new file" for .gitkeep and .gitignore.
